---
import Demo from '../../layouts/Demo.astro';
---

<Demo slug="width-axis">
  <div class="stage panel" data-stage>
    <p class="stage__loading" data-status>Loading the WebAssembly module…</p>

    <div class="stage__body" data-body hidden>
      <section class="block">
        <h2>1 · The published table, recomputed live</h2>
        <p class="prose">
          These are the repository's own three corpora — the Fibonacci essay, a Go source file, and
          a repeating Fibonacci byte pattern — run through the same experiment that
          <code>REPORT_STRUCTURAL.md</code> publishes. A test in
          <code>internal/wasmapi</code> diffs the live result against that document's transcription
          on every build, so if the two ever disagree the build fails.
        </p>

        <div class="matrix__scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Dilation rate matrix, scrollable">
          <table data-matrix class="matrix">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">
              Dilation rate by adjacency width and input class, live and published
            </caption>
            <thead>
              <tr data-matrix-head></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody data-matrix-body></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

  <p class="table-key">
    <span><span class="key key--live" aria-hidden="true"></span> live, from this page's WebAssembly run</span>
    <span><span class="key key--pub" aria-hidden="true"></span> published, transcribed from REPORT_STRUCTURAL.md</span>
    <span><span class="key key--best" aria-hidden="true"></span> most sensitive class at that width</span>
  </p>

        <p class="verify-line" data-verify></p>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <h2>2 · The falsification, running</h2>
        <p class="prose">
          Here is the whole claim in one assertion: dilation counts are <strong>non-increasing in
          width for every possible input</strong>, because widths 1, 2 and 3 test for a 1-run of
          length at least 2, 3 and 4, so the event sets are nested. Press the button and it runs
          that assertion over randomised streams.
        </p>

        <div class="falsify">
          <div class="falsify__controls">
            <label class="field field--narrow">
              <span class="label">Random streams</span>
              <input type="number" data-streams min="100" max="20000" step="100" value="2000" />
            </label>
            <label class="field field--narrow">
              <span class="label">Seed</span>
              <input type="number" data-seed value="20240914" />
            </label>
            <button type="button" data-run class="btn btn--primary">Run the assertion</button>
          </div>

          <div class="falsify__result" data-result hidden>
            <p class="verdict">
              <span class="verdict__big num" data-violations>—</span>
              <span class="verdict__label">violations</span>
            </p>
            <p class="verdict__note" data-verdict-note></p>
            <div class="falsify__rates" data-rates></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="block">
        <h2>3 · What survives the retraction</h2>
        <div class="survivors">
          <article class="survivor">
            <p class="label">Survives</p>
            <h3>The sensitivity ranking shifts</h3>
            <p>
              Width 1 is most sensitive to prose; widths 2 and 3 are most sensitive to code. That is
              a real observation. It follows <em>from</em> the nesting rather than being evidence of
              anything, and it is a consequence worth keeping.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="survivor">
            <p class="label">Survives</p>
            <h3>Regular input vanishes entirely</h3>
            <p>
              The repeating Fibonacci byte pattern never produces three consecutive ones, so its
              dilation rate is exactly <strong>0.0000</strong> at width 2 and above. A wider window
              suppresses a regular signal rather than merely being less sensitive to it.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="survivor">
            <p class="label">Survives</p>
            <h3>Code is about 14× burstier than prose</h3>
            <p>
              Windowed dilation variance at width 1: 0.000222 for code against 0.000016 for prose.
              Code's profile is bursty in time; prose is uniform. This is the substantive finding
              in the report.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="prose withdrawn">
          <strong>Withdrawn.</strong> “The transponder array is a multi-detector sensor, not a
          multi-fingerprint wrapper.” The three transponders see identical event
          <em>structure</em>; only their sketch fingerprints differ. There are no orthogonal axes
          and no 2-dimensional parameter space. And the threshold axis is untested on these corpora
          — no marker fires in any of the 9 configurations, so no independence conclusion is
          available from them at all.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="notes">
    <section class="note retract-note">
      <p>
        <strong>Why this is the page's best artefact.</strong> A wrong claim that gets retracted in
        public, with the assertion that would catch it coming back, is worth more to a reader than
        another working demo. The alternative — quietly dropping the claim — would leave no way to
        tell the difference between a project that was never wrong and one that was wrong and
        covered it up.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="note claim-note">
      <p>
        <strong>Also worth noting.</strong> The prose-versus-code shift is partly an encoding
        artefact: the width-2 and width-3 sensitivity is driven by which ASCII bytes contain long
        one-runs (<code>|</code>, <code>}</code>, <code>~</code>, <code>&gt;</code> all have runs
        of 4 to 6), and Go source is dense in exactly those characters.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Demo>

<script>
  import { invoke } from '../../lib/fib';
  import { need, needAll, setStatus } from '../../lib/ui';

  interface Cell {
    width: number;
    dilations: string;
    dilateRate: number;
    markers: string;
    markerRate: number;
    mostSensitive: boolean;
  }
  interface Row {
    label: string;
    bitCount: number;
    oneDensity: number;
    residual: number;
    cells: Cell[];
  }
  interface CorpusOut {
    widths: number[];
    classes: Row[];
    published: Row[];
    windowBits: number;
    note: string;
    markersAllZero: boolean;
    corpusBytes: Record<string, number>;
  }
  interface NestingOut {
    streams: number;
    violations: number;
    firstFailure?: string;
    seed: number;
    widths: number[];
    strictlyRanked: number;
    tiedAtTop: number;
    meanRatePerWidth: number[];
    note: string;
  }

  const status = need<HTMLElement>('[data-status]');
  const body = need<HTMLElement>('[data-body]');
  const headRow = need<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-matrix-head]');
  const tbody = need<HTMLTableSectionElement>('[data-matrix-body]');
  const verifyLine = need<HTMLElement>('[data-verify]');
  const streamsInput = need<HTMLInputElement>('[data-streams]');
  const seedInput = need<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]');
  const runBtn = need<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-run]');
  const resultBox = need<HTMLElement>('[data-result]');
  const violationsEl = need<HTMLElement>('[data-violations]');
  const verdictNote = need<HTMLElement>('[data-verdict-note]');
  const ratesBox = need<HTMLElement>('[data-rates]');

  async function boot(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      await invoke('fsvm.meta', {});
      body.hidden = false;
      status.hidden = true;
      await loadMatrix();
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus(status, (err as Error).message, 'error');
    }
  }

  async function loadMatrix(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      const { data } = await invoke<CorpusOut>('structural.corpus', {});
      renderMatrix(data);
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus(status, (err as Error).message, 'error');
    }
  }

  function renderMatrix(d: CorpusOut): void {
    const classNames = d.classes.map((c) => c.label);

    // Two header rows: the class name spans its two columns, which are the live
    // run and the published figure. Rendering "w-class prose" twice, or
    // labelling both columns identically, makes the comparison unreadable --
    // and the whole point of the table is the comparison.
    const topRow = el('tr');
    topRow.append(el('th', { scope: 'col', rowspan: '2', class: 'corner' }, 'width'));
    for (const name of classNames) {
      const th = el('th', { scope: 'colgroup', colspan: '2', class: 'grouped' }, name);
      topRow.append(th);
    }
    const subRow = el('tr', { class: 'sub' });
    for (const _ of classNames) {
      subRow.append(
        el('th', { scope: 'col', class: 'subhead' }, 'live'),
        el('th', { scope: 'col', class: 'subhead subhead--pub' }, 'published'),
      );
    }
    // Swap the placeholder header row out for the two real rows.
    const thead = headRow.closest('thead');
    if (thead) {
      thead.replaceChildren(topRow, subRow);
    }

    const rows = d.widths.map((w) => {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      const cells: HTMLElement[] = [];
      cells.push(el('td', { class: 'rowhead num' }, `w=${w}`));

      for (const c of d.classes) {
        const cell = c.cells.find((x) => x.width === w);
        cells.push(
          el(
            'td',
            {
              class: `cell num${cell?.mostSensitive ? ' cell--best' : ''}`,
              'data-rate': cell ? cell.dilateRate.toFixed(4) : '',
            },
            cell ? cell.dilateRate.toFixed(4) : '—',
          ),
        );
        const pub = d.published.find((p) => p.label === `${c.label} (published)`);
        const pv = pub?.cells.find((x) => x.width === w);
        cells.push(el('td', { class: 'cell cell--pub num' }, pv ? pv.dilateRate.toFixed(4) : '—'));
      }
      tr.replaceChildren(...cells);
      return tr;
    });
    tbody.replaceChildren(...rows);

    // Compare live against published, and say so on the page rather than
    // letting the reader do the subtraction.
    //
    // Round the live rate to the report's four decimals *before* comparing.
    // The synthetic control at width 1 is 384/12288 = 0.03125 exactly, which
    // is 0.00005 from the published 0.0313 — precisely on the tolerance
    // boundary, and floating-point error tips it over. Comparing raw rates
    // against a four-decimal transcription reports a false mismatch there. The
    // Go test rounds first for the same reason.
    const round4 = (v: number) => Math.round(v * 10000) / 10000;
    let mismatches = 0;
    let compared = 0;
    const mismatchList: string[] = [];
    for (const c of d.classes) {
      const pub = d.published.find((p) => p.label === `${c.label} (published)`);
      if (!pub) continue;
      for (const pc of pub.cells) {
        const live = c.cells.find((x) => x.width === pc.width);
        if (!live) continue;
        compared++;
        if (Math.abs(round4(live.dilateRate) - pc.dilateRate) > 1e-9) {
          mismatches++;
          mismatchList.push(`${c.label} w=${pc.width} live ${round4(live.dilateRate).toFixed(4)} vs published ${pc.dilateRate.toFixed(4)}`);
        }
      }
    }

    const bytes = d.classes
      .map((c) => `${c.label} ${d.corpusBytes[c.label]?.toLocaleString('en-US')} B`)
      .join(' · ');

    verifyLine.replaceChildren(
      el('span', { class: 'tag tag-verified' }, mismatches === 0 ? 'Verified' : 'Mismatch'),
      document.createTextNode(
        ` ${compared - mismatches} of ${compared} live rates match ` +
          `REPORT_STRUCTURAL.md to four decimals. Corpus: ${bytes}.`,
      ),
      el('span', { class: 'verify-line__extra' },
        d.markersAllZero
          ? ' No marker fired in any of the 9 configurations, which is why the threshold axis is untested rather than proven independent.'
          : ' At least one marker fired, so the second-axis retraction would no longer hold.'),
    );
    if (mismatchList.length) {
      verifyLine.append(el('span', { class: 'verify-line__extra verify-line__extra--bad' }, mismatchList.join(' · ')));
    }
    verifyLine.dataset.kind = mismatches === 0 ? 'ok' : 'error';
  }

  function el<K extends keyof HTMLElementTagNameMap>(
    tag: K,
    attrs: Record<string, string> = {},
    ...children: Array<Node | string>
  ): HTMLElementTagNameMap[K] {
    const node = document.createElement(tag);
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(attrs)) node.setAttribute(k, v);
    for (const c of children) node.append(c);
    return node;
  }

  /* ---- The live falsification ---- */
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    runBtn.disabled = true;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Running…';
    try {
      const { data } = await invoke<NestingOut>('structural.nesting', {
        streams: Number(streamsInput.value) || 2000,
        seed: Number(seedInput.value) || 20240914,
      });

      resultBox.hidden = false;
      violationsEl.textContent = String(data.violations);
      resultBox.dataset.kind = data.violations === 0 ? 'ok' : 'error';

      const tiedPct = data.streams ? (data.tiedAtTop / data.streams) * 100 : 0;
      verdictNote.textContent =
        data.violations === 0
          ? `Held on all ${data.streams.toLocaleString('en-US')} randomised streams. ` +
            `Mean dilation rate fell from ${data.meanRatePerWidth[0]?.toFixed(4)} at width 1 to ` +
            `${data.meanRatePerWidth.at(-1)?.toFixed(4)} at width ${data.widths.at(-1)}, as nesting forces. ` +
            `${tiedPct.toFixed(0)}% of streams tied at the top, which is exactly the artefact that made ` +
            `the original report read as "not strictly monotonic".`
          : `${data.violations.toLocaleString('en-US')} streams violated the invariant, first at index ` +
            `${data.firstFailure}. If this number is ever above zero, the claim on this page is wrong.`;

      ratesBox.replaceChildren(
        ...data.widths.map((w, i) => {
          const div = document.createElement('div');
          div.className = 'rate';
          div.append(
            el('span', { class: 'rate__w num' }, `w=${w}`),
            el('span', { class: 'rate__v num' }, data.meanRatePerWidth[i].toFixed(4)),
          );
          return div;
        }),
      );
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus(status, (err as Error).message, 'error');
    } finally {
      runBtn.disabled = false;
      runBtn.textContent = 'Run the assertion';
    }
  });

  void boot();
</script>

<style>
  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  .stage {
    padding: 1.6rem 1.75rem 1.75rem;
  }
  .stage__loading {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    padding: 2rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stage__loading[data-kind='error'] {
    color: var(--retract-lit);
    text-align: left;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  .stage__body[data-kind='error'] {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--retract);
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }

  .block + .block {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    padding-top: 2.25rem;
    border-top: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  .prose {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .prose.withdrawn {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--retract);
    background: var(--retract-wash);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
  }

  /* ---- Matrix ---- */
  .matrix__scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    box-shadow: var(--sunk-sm);
  }
  .matrix {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
  }
  .matrix th,
  .matrix td {
    padding: 0.55rem 0.85rem;
    text-align: right;
    border-bottom: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .matrix thead th {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 600;
    position: sticky;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  /* Row 1: the class name, spanning its live/published pair. */
  .matrix thead tr:first-child th {
    top: 0;
    padding-block: 0.5rem 0.35rem;
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .matrix thead tr:first-child .corner {
    text-align: left;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .matrix thead .grouped {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--brass);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    border-bottom: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
  }
  /* Row 2: which column is which. */
  .matrix thead tr.sub th {
    top: 1.75rem;
    padding-block: 0.3rem 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .matrix thead .subhead--pub {
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .matrix tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .rowhead {
    color: var(--brass-lit);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: left;
  }
  /* The published column is a transcription, so it recedes. The live column is
     the measurement and reads at full strength, which is what makes the
     comparison legible at a glance rather than by reading every pair. */
  .cell {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .cell--pub {
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  /* The most-sensitive cell per class is marked three ways: colour, weight, and
     a ring. Colour alone would fail WCAG 1.4.1. */
  .cell--best {
    color: var(--verify-lit);
    font-weight: 700;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--verify);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
  }
  .cell--best::after {
    content: ' ◂';
    font-size: 0.7em;
    vertical-align: 0.15em;
  }

  /* Legend for the table, so the three column styles are named rather than
     left to be inferred. */
  .table-key {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .table-key > span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .key {
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .key--live {
    background: var(--ink);
  }
  .key--pub {
    background: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .key--best {
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--verify);
  }

  .verify-line {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.83rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.6;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .verify-line__extra {
    display: block;
    flex-basis: 100%;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }
  .verify-line__extra--bad {
    color: var(--retract-lit);
  }

  /* ---- Falsify ---- */
  .falsify__controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-end;
  }
  .field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .field--narrow {
    flex: 0 0 9rem;
  }
  .btn--primary {
    color: var(--brass-lit);
    border-color: var(--brass-dim);
  }

  .falsify__result {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    box-shadow: var(--sunk-sm);
  }
  .falsify__result[data-kind='ok'] {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--verify) 50%, var(--rule));
  }
  .falsify__result[data-kind='error'] {
    border-color: var(--retract);
  }

  .verdict {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .verdict__big {
    font-size: 2.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--verify);
  }
  .falsify__result[data-kind='error'] .verdict__big {
    color: var(--retract);
  }
  .verdict__label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }
  .verdict__note {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  .falsify__rates {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
  }
  .rate {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.85rem;
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .rate__w {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .rate__v {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--brass);
  }

  /* ---- Survivors ---- */
  .survivors {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr));
  }
  .survivor {
    padding: 1.15rem 1.3rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--verify);
  }
  .survivor h3 {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .survivor p:last-child {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .notes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 20rem), 1fr));
    align-items: start;
  }
  .notes .note {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }
</style>
